2026-09-26T03:53:14.4861690Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4861865Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862089Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862167Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862276Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862349Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862448Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862525Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862623Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862710Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862801Z             return x + 1
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862877Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4862948Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863044Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863139Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863211Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863288Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863375Z     To execute it::
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863446Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863530Z         $ pytest
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863694Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863787Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863859Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4863959Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864036Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864175Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864351Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864430Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864528Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864616Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864706Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864804Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864875Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4864985Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4865138Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4865210Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4865288Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866159Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866240Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866311Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866394Z     Features
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866478Z     --------
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4866551Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867029Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867105Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867301Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867590Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867691Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4867768Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868026Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868194Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868274Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868535Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868628Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868704Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868800Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4868870Z     
2026-09-26T03:53:14.4869470Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
